  <h4>Distribute Stat Points</h4>
  <p>
    Players have 16 Stat Points to distribute among the four Stats. Each Stat must have at least 1 Stat Point allocated to it. During Character Creation, no Stat may be increased
    to a value higher than 6.
  </p>
  <p>The starting stat dice is D6.</p>
  <h4>Record Other Values</h4>
  <p>
    <span class="charbold">Physical Defense</span>
    score is equal to their Edge Stat + 2 + any bonuses granted by Skills or other rules (minimum value of 5, regardless of their Edge stat and other bonuses).
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="charbold">Sorcery Defense</span>
    is equal to their Wits Stat + 2 + any bonuses granted by Skills or other rules (minimum value of 5, regardless of their Wits stat and other bonuses).
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="charbold">Life Points: </span>
    their starting (and maximum) Life Points is the double of the Grit Stat + the number of Base Life Points from the Origin.
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="charbold">Stamina Points</span>
    are equal to their Grit Stat.
  </p>
  <p>
    The
    <span class="charbold">Flex Die</span>
    starts as a D10.
  </p>
  <h4>Choose Starting Skills</h4>
  <p>
    A PC may spend their starting 3 XP on any Skills from the Starting Skills table below, as well as any Sorcery Skills from the Sorcery Disciplines that the PC’s Origin allows.
  </p><p>The skills can be either drag-and-dropped from the
    <em>Skills</em>
    and
    <em>Spells</em>
    folders, or created on the character sheet by clicking on the
    <i class="fas fa-plus"></i>
    icon.</p>
